cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use IntonaSphere AI in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "IntonaSphere AI: A Transcription and Praat-Based Prosody Analysis Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  IntonaSphere AI is an open-source Streamlit application and Python toolkit that
  combines automatic speech transcription (faster-whisper), multilingual phonetic
  transcription (phonemizer/eSpeak-NG, Epitran), and Praat-based acoustic analysis
  (via Parselmouth) for research on intonation and prosody. It supports
  audio/TextGrid pair processing, token-level extraction of F0, semitone-normalized
  pitch measures, final slope, intensity, duration, plateau duration and rule-based
  final-contour classification, batch extraction for PFC-style corpora, transcription
  accuracy testing (WER), and export to CSV, Excel, DOCX, PDF and SRT. Version 0.2.0 adds
  a command-line research pipeline: automatic WebMAUS alignment, final-syllable acoustic
  cues with five contour classes, F_ToBI proposal TextGrids, a 28-column dataset with its
  codebook, run comparison, and Praat scripts that re-measure the values.
